or VTT?","vtt_map_resize_text":"We can adjust the current page's size to fit this image or resize this image to fit the page.","vtt_map_extra_space_text":"It looks like there's some extra space. Adjust page size to match image size?","vtt_map_resize_adjust":"Adjust Page Size","vtt_map_resize_fit":"Fit to Page","vtt_map_resize_text_populated":"This image is larger than the current page. If you would like we can resize this image to fit the page.","vtt_map_resize_deny":"Place As Is","vtt_map_resize_yes":"Yes","vtt_map_resize_no":"No","vtt_resize_asset_title":"Set Token Default Size","vtt_resize_asset_text":"Enter the height and width in grid cells you would like this token to be ","token_bars_hover":"Hover to show nameplate and bar overlay (tokens + Map Pins)","resize_maps_option":"Disable auto sizing of assets dropped on the Map Layer","debug_images":"Debug broken images (requires refresh)","transparent_barrier_block_movement_off":"To use Transparent Barriers you must enable Restrict Movement. Would you like us to turn it on for you?","block_movement_off":"Restrict Player Token Movement?","pdf_is_still_being_processed":"PDF is still being processed","apply-token-defaults-text":"All {{0}} tokens representing {{1}} on {{2}} page(s) will be overwritten! This includes overwriting the existing tokens' size, attributes, and markers. Are you sure?","apply-token-defaults-title":"Overwrite {{0}} tokens?","token_bar_linked_tooltip":"This token bar is linked to a character attribute.","character_not_in_journal":"A selected character is not in your journal.","win_color_desc":"Window Line Color","locked_window":"Locked Window","opened":"Opened","window_block_movement_off":"To use Windows you must enable Restrict Movement. Would you like us to turn it on for you?","door_block_movement_off":"To use Doors you must enable Restrict Movement. Would you like us to turn it on for you?","line_color":"Line Color","window":"Window","door":"Door","secret":"Secret","shuttered":"Curtains","locked":"Locked","door_tour_1_title":"You can now place doors! ","door_tour_1_text":"Place interactive doors that can be opened by players with a single click. Or, 'lock' the door and see what your players do to tackle the challenge.","door_tour_2_title":"Door placement is flexible.","door_tour_2_text":"You can drop doors on any layer. Try placing your first door!","door_tour_3_title":"Adjust your doors on the Dynamic Lighting layer","door_tour_3_text":"On the dynamic lighting layer, you can move the handles around to arrange your door as needed. Try it now.","door_tour_4_title":"Keep secrets from your players ","door_tour_4_text":"After selecting a door you placed, you can make your doors secret for players until you reveal them during a game. Try making your door secret!","door_tour_5_title":"Your players can interact with doors!","door_tour_5_text":"When a door is on the token layer and isn't secret, your players can click the door icon to open it. You can lock doors to block movement and stop your players from opening them.","back":"Back","framerate_limit":"Maximum frames per second","framerate_uncapped":"Uncapped (browser default)","tut_title_1":"Welcome to Roll20!","tut_title_2":"Moving Around","tut_title_3":"The Toolbar","tut_title_4":"Page Toolbar","tut_title_5":"Drawing Tools","tut_title_6":"Chat","tut_title_7":"Journal","tut_title_8":"Layers","tut_title_9":"Dynamic Lighting","tut_title_10":"Keep Exploring!","tut_text_1_pt_1":"Welcome to The Starship Quantum Roll! This vessel will be your guide to the wonderful world of Roll20.","tut_text_1_pt_2":"Let's have a quick look around to get started. Zoom in using this slider, or use the eyeglass tool over in your toolbar on the left for a closer look.","tut_text_2_pt_1":"Great! Now that you have an idea of the layout, it's time to do some walking around. You can right-click and drag to pan around the map or navigate using a token.","tut_text_2_pt_2":"Select the crewmember (Your Character) on the map and drag them around to move. You can also use the directional arrows on your keyboard to move around the grid.","tut_text_3_pt_1":"Awesome! But moving around's just the beginning. There are so many things you can do in Roll20. The home for all your actions is the toolbar.","tut_text_3_pt_2":"You already know what the magnifying glass does—that helps you get a better look at the map.","tut_text_3_pt_3":"Try out some of the other buttons now and see if you can roll a die or measure the distance between two squares.","tut_text_4_pt_1":"What good is a spaceship that can't take you to other worlds?","tut_text_4_pt_2":"Click the blue Page Toolbar icon at the top to change maps.","tut_text_4_pt_3":"Right now, you're the GM—the captain of this ship, if you will. Lucky you! The GM controls what the players can see. By dragging the red player ribbon to a map, a GM can bring the players to that map instantly.","tut_text_4_pt_4":"Sometimes, you'll want to visit a page alone to plan ahead—that's easy! Just click to that page yourself without bringing the player ribbon over and you can take a quick peek.","tut_text_4_pt_5":"Let's hop over to the Dashboard now. Click “Next” once you're there.","tut_text_5_pt_1":"Welcome to the Dashboard! This world was built with Roll20 drawing tools and animations, but if you ask us, it's missing that personal touch.","tut_text_5_pt_2":"Access the drawing tools by clicking the paintbrush on the toolbar and selecting 'Freehand.' Then, add a doodle to the Dashboard! Keep it PG, folks.","tut_text_6_pt_1":"Beautifully done! You've got the pictures down pat. Now, let's chat about chat!","tut_text_6_pt_2":"These icons on the right of your screen let you access Chat (visible by all players), your Art Library, your Journal, the Jukebox, your Collections, and your Settings. For now, click the speech bubble icon to access Chat. You already know how to roll dice from the toolbar, but you can roll dice here, too!","tut_text_6_pt_3":"You can roll a 20-sided die by typing in /roll 1d20 or /r 1d20, or whisper to a player by typing in /w [name] [message]. Whispering means that only you and the player you've whispered to will see your message. You can't whisper right now, since you're currently the only one in this game.","tut_text_7_pt_1":"Dice? Check. Movement? Check. Doodles? Double-check. You've got most of the basics, now—let's talk about character sheets.","tut_text_7_pt_2":"Your character sheets are kept safely inside your Journal. Click the Journal tab and open the 'Your Character' character sheet. Inside, we'll show you how a character sheet works in Roll20.","tut_text_8_pt_1":"Much like a delicious parfait, Roll20 has <strong>layers</strong>. Four layers, in fact: the <strong>Object & Tokens layer</strong> for game pieces you'll interact with in the course of play, the <strong>Map & Background layer</strong> for objects that will remain static throughout the game, the <strong>GM Info overlay layer</strong> that's for Game Master's eyes only, and the <strong>Dynamic Lighting layer</strong>, which we'll explore now.","tut_text_8_pt_2":"Navigate to 'The Character Vaults' map using the page menu. Once you're there, open the Dynamic Lighting layer using the cube icon in the left-side toolbar.","tut_text_9_pt_1":"Dynamic Lighting is a fancy Roll20-specific system that updates players' lines of sight in real time. That means that players can only see the parts of the map that their characters would be able to see.","tut_text_9_pt_2":"You can adjust things like sightlines, field of vision, coloring of light, and more, all using Dynamic Lighting.","tut_text_9_pt_3":"This space is your playground to try Dynamic Lighting out. No changes you make here will save, and you're free to experiment as you wish!","tut_text_9_pt_4":"If you want to see what a player will see with Dynamic Lighting, navigate to the Objects and Tokens layer and click on the 'Your Character' token then press Ctrl+L (Cmd+L on Macs). That will show you the map from their perspective.","tut_text_10_pt_1":"There are so many more things to see and discover here. Once you've explored to your heart's content, check out our <a href='https://app.roll20.net/lfg/search/'>Looking for Group</a> feature to find a group to play with. If you want to dive deeper and master your maps, check out some of our <a href='https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLTj75n3v9eTljjooh-nIr_LFAeHatTeI4'>video tutorials</a>","tut_text_10_pt_2":"None of your changes in this game will save, and you can't invite other players. When you're ready to move on and make your first real game with other players, head over to the <a href='https://app.roll20.net/campaigns/new'>Create New Game page</a>!","tut_text_10_pt_3":"Happy rolling!","realtime_chat_tour_1_title":"Check out <%= chat_tech %>!","realtime_chat_tour_1_text":"Your GM has enabled <%= chat_tech %> for this game.  To make sure your settings are configured properly to chat, head over to the Settings tab by clicking the ‘cogwheel’ in the top right of the screen.","realtime_chat_tour_2_title":"Head to the Audio & Video section","realtime_chat_tour_2_text":"Now, open the ‘Audio & Video’ section by clicking it here.","realtime_chat_tour_3_title":"Configure your settings","realtime_chat_tour_3_text":"<p>Use <strong>Audio Input Source</strong> and <strong>Video Input Source</strong> to change the microphone and camera used respectively. To disable sending voice and/or video altogether, set your preferences using the button group <strong>Others can hear or see</strong> accordingly. Changing the size and/or location of player frames can be done in the <strong>Video Display</strong> tab. For all other details, open the related Help Centre article using the link below.","realtime_chat_tour_3_btn_secondary":"<a href='https://help.roll20.net/hc/articles/360039223594-Video-and-Voice-Chat-Troubleshooting#VideoandVoiceChatTroubleshooting-CheckMySettings'>Open Help Center article</a>","dismiss":"Dismiss","next":"Next","device_permis