st your measurements to the party, or keep them secret as you plot your next move!","end_tour":"Done","compendium:categories":"Categories","compendium:searchRelatedCategories":"Related Categories","compendium:searchPlaceholder":"Search Compendium","compendium:searchNoResultsHeader":"No Matching Results","compendium:searchNoResultsText":"No results found for {searchString}","compendium:searchNoResultsNotSeeingSomething":"Not seeing something you own? <a href='https://help.roll20.net/hc/articles/35038211600919-Compendium-Products-Not-Appearing-In-Game'>Click here</a> for instructions.","compendium:networkErrorHeader":"This was a bad brew!","compendium:networkErrorText":"Our connection got mixed up - and not in a good way. Go ahead and retry.","compendium:emptyCategoryErrorText":"There doesn't seem to be any content in this category.","compendium:noContentAvailableErrorText":"You do not have access to any content for {ruleSystem}.","compendium:retryButton":"Retry","compendium:goBackButton":"Go Back","compendium:blockedCompendiumsNotificationPlayer":"This game has blocked compendiums. Talk to your GM to request changes.","compendium:blockedCompendiumsNotificationGM":"This game has some compendiums blocked. To make changes go to ","compendium:filterNoResultsText":"No results found for current filter combination.","compendium:filterRetry":"Retry with different filters","compendium:filters":"Filters","compendium:clearFilters":"Clear","compendium:applyFilters":"Apply","compendium:cancel":"Cancel","compendium:clearAllFilters":"Clear All","marketplaceCTA1":"Unlock more character options","marketplaceCTA2":"See everything for {gameSystem}","marketplaceCTA3":"Unlock Characters","shared_journal_entry_with_players_notification":"Shared with {{0}} players","shared_journal_entry_with_player_notification":"Shared with {{0}}","shared_journal_entry_with_all_players_notification":"Shared with all players","shared_journal_entry_notification":"Shared entry","shared_journal_entry_notification_exit":"Dismiss","new_page_sequenced":"New Page {{0}}","new_folder_sequenced":"New Folder {{0}}","new_scrawl_sequenced":"My Dungeon Scrawl {{0}}","scrawl_socket_retry":"Warning: Dungeon Scrawl Cannot connect at this time. Please retry.","scrawl_socket_error":"Warning: Dungeon Scrawl Errored. Please retry","new_compendium":"New Compendium","new_compendium_info":"Toggling New Compendium will cause a page reload.","select_all":"Select All","compendium_tour_1_title":"Navigating through the compendium ","compendium_tour_1_text":"The Compendium allows you to access rules from a variety of systems you own or have access to.","compendium_tour_2_title":"Selecting a category","compendium_tour_2_text":"Selecting a category will populate a list of items from those systems.","compendium_tour_3_title":"Viewing more information","compendium_tour_3_text":"If you click on the card, a pop out window will display the description of the item.","compendium_tour_4_title":"Expanding information cards","compendium_tour_4_text":"To save on screen space, you can also view the content by clicking on the down arrow when available.","compendium_tour_5_title":"Adding to your sheet","compendium_tour_5_text":"You can directly drag and drop items to be added to your character sheet.","compendium_tour_6_title":"Using the compendium search ","compendium_tour_6_text":"Unsure of the category? Use the search bar to find results instantly!","compendium_tour_7_title":"Using filters","compendium_tour_7_text":"Some compendiums have certain categories with a filter option, which allows you to search for specific details.","compendium_tour_8_title":"Ready to unlock more content? ","compendium_tour_8_text":"Click the browse marketplace link below to see all the compendium content available to you!","compendium_8_cta":"Browse Marketplace","page_folders_tour_1_title":"Check Out Page Folders ","page_folders_tour_1_text":"We're excited to announce that Page Folders and the Party Toolbox are now the default for all users in all campaigns. Open the page menu to check it out.","page_folders_tour_2_title":"Add a page folder ","page_folders_tour_2_text":"Create your first folder by pressing the create folder button. Note, you can also drag a page onto another page to create a folder.","page_folders_tour_3_title":"Organization is key ","page_folders_tour_3_text":"Click into your folder and create pages as needed! After you add a folder, you can also expand \"My Folders\" on the left side to see a list view. Dragging a page onto a folder in the folder list - or a breadcrumb - moves it up a level.","page_folders_tour_4_title":"Move, split and track ","page_folders_tour_4_text":"Our party toolbox allows you to move your party around as needed. You can drag your party ribbon around, create new parties, or move individual players.","page_folders_tour_5_title":"Proceed to party ","page_folders_tour_5_text":"Track your split parties with their ribbons, and regroup split parties easily with a single \"Regroup All\" button.","page_folder_are_you_sure":"Are you sure?","gm_layer":"GM Layer","gm_foreground":"GM Foreground","gm_darkness":"GM Darkness","layer_opacity":"Layer Opacity","foreground_visible_toggle":"Show Foreground to Players","skip_link_to_page_menu":"Skip to the page menu","skip_link_to_chat_tab":"Skip to the chat tab","character_editor_ownership_error":"You cannot remove a character's owner from 'Can Be Edited & Controlled By' or from 'In Player's Journal'.","tutorial_slide_1_title":"Roll20 Awaits!","tutorial_slide_1_text":"Welcome aboard The Starship Quantum Roll, your guide to the Roll20 universe. Join us as we navigate the cosmos together, exploring Roll20's stellar features designed to enhance your tabletop roleplaying experience.","tutorial_slide_1_next":"Let's explore!","tutorial_slide_2_title":"Moving Around","tutorial_slide_2_text":"Now that you're strapped into the captain's chair, it's time to master the art of navigation. Right-click and drag your mouse to <span class='Roll20Icon'>pan</span> <strong>pan</strong> around the starship map - or use the scrollbars. <strong>Zoom</strong> in and out using the zoom tool at the top right, or hold Alt while using your scroll wheel. Press on the bullseye <span class='Roll20Icon'>target</span> to <strong>recenter the map.</strong>","tutorial_slide_3_title":"Tokens and Characters","tutorial_slide_3_text":"Many games use <strong>tokens</strong> to represent characters &#128373;&#65039;&#8205;&#9792;&#65039; (or monsters!!!) <span class='Roll20Icon'>cursor</span> Select the token called 'your character' and drag them around. (You can also use the directional arrows on your keyboard to move your character across the grid with precision.)","tutorial_slide_4_title":"The Toolbar","tutorial_slide_4_text":"Moving around is just the beginning. The toolbar is your hub for many Roll20 actions. Try using the <strong>freehand tool</strong> <span class='Roll20Icon'>drawBrush</span> to draw some doodles, or for those of you who are more precise, use the <strong>measure tool</strong> <span class='Roll20Icon'>measure</span> to measure the distance between 'Your character' and various objects on the spaceship. Fun, right?","tutorial_slide_5_title":"Cool Tools!","tutorial_slide_5_text":"Use the <strong>Effects <span class='Roll20Icon'>wandSparkle</span></strong> tool to create dynamic visual effects at a click of a button and bring your stories to life! The <strong>Hide / Reveal Mask Tool <span class='Roll20Icon'>mask</span></strong> can be used to manually hide a map - or parts of a map - from players. <strong>Dynamic Lighting <span class='Roll20Icon'>dynamicLightingSun</span></strong> is a pro feature to update player’s line of sight in real time as they explore the map. These tools are updated in Jumpgate.","tutorial_slide_6_title":"Page Menu","tutorial_slide_6_text":"What good is a spaceship if you can't hop to other worlds? The <span class='Roll20Icon'>pageList</span> <strong>Page Folders menu</strong> allows you, the GM, to organize and change maps. Add pages or folders, drag pages or folders in and out of folders to change levels, and see a full list view. Open up the page menu, then change maps from this spaceship, 'The Quantum Roll', to the page called 'Dashboard.'","tutorial_slide_7_title":"Moving your Players","tutorial_slide_7_text":"The GM controls what players can see. Right now, the <strong>player ribbon</strong> is on 'The Quantum Roll,' meaning that players in your game can see and interact with that page. Grabbing and dragging the player ribbon from 'The Quantum Roll' to the 'Dashboard' page - or navigating to “Dashboard” page, clicking the “more icon”, and electing to “Move Party Ribbon Here” - would bring your players to that page instantly.<br><br> Of course, this is hypothetical, as you are alone in this universe for now.","tutorial_slide_8_title":"Sidebar Chat","tutorial_slide_8_text":"The sidebar has <strong>Chat</strong>, your <strong>Art Library</strong>, your <strong>Journal</strong>, the <strong>Jukebox</strong>, your <strong>Collection</strong> of plugins and macros, and <strong>Game Settings</strong>. <br><br><span class='Roll20Icon'>chatTab</span> <strong>Chat</strong> is the first tab in the right hand sidebar. You can use chat to type messages to everyone, whisper to specific people, view character sheet roll results, or even roll dice. Check out what chat can do here. <br><br> For now, type /roll 1d20  or /r 1d20 to roll one twenty sided die and see the automagic result.","tutorial_slide_9_title":"The Journal","tutorial_slide_9_text":"In the sidebar, you will also find your <span class='Roll20Icon'>journalTab</span> <strong>Journal</strong>. This is the information hub for your game, where you keep your <strong>character sheets</strong> and game <strong>handouts</strong>. You - the GM - control who can see what by editing the permissions. <br><br> The journal in this game already contains one character sheet - Your Character (which is linked to the <strong>token</strong> you have been interacting with!) - and three notes about different locations across the universe- Tinyton, Rolltopia, and Siville. <br><br> Open up the note about 'tinyton' and read its secret in the GM Notes section. 'Show to players' will open the note on your players' screens, but will not show them anything in the GM notes section!","tutorial_slide_10_title":"Layers","tutorial_slide_10_text":"Much like a delicious parfait, Roll20 has layers. Four layers, in fact... <br><br>* <strong>Object & Tokens layer:</strong> for game pieces and tokens that you and your players interact with in the course of play. <br>* <strong>GM Info Overlay layer:</strong> for Game Master's eyes only - to keep your secrets safe and tidy until the right time.  <br>* <strong>Dynamic Lighting layer:</strong> a layer for lighting lines to allow you - the GM - to control what players can see as they explore your intricate maps. <br>* <strong>Map & Background layer:</strong> for background images and objects that will remain static throughout the game. <br><br> Navigate to <strong>'The Character Vaults'</strong> map using the page menu. Once you're there, <strong>switch layers</strong> from the <span class='Roll20Icon'>layerToken</span> Token and Object layer to the <span class='Roll20Icon'>layerLight</span> <strong>Dynamic Lighting layer</strong>; you'll notice light lines along the dungeon walls that weren't visible before...","tutorial_slide_11_title":"Dynamic Lighting","tutorial_slide_11_text":"Dynamic Lighting is a powerful, Roll20-specific system that updates players' lines of sight in real time. That means that <strong>players can only see the parts of the map that their character tokens would be able to see.</strong> You can adjust things like sightlines, field of vision, coloring of light, and more, all using Dynamic Lighting. <br><br>If you want to see what a player will see with Dynamic Lighting, you can! On this page you can drag and drop a character from your journal onto the objects and tokens layer, then press Ctrl+L to see the map from their perspective!","tutorial_slide_12_title":"Keep exploring!","tutorial_slide_12_text":"There are so many more things to see and discover here. Once you've explored to your heart's content, check out <a href='https://help.roll20.net/hc/articles/360037773373' target='blank'><strong>character sheet tips</strong></a> or some of our <a href='https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLTj75n3v9eTljjooh-nIr_LFAeHatTeI4' target='blank'><strong>video tutorials</strong></a>. <br><br> None of your changes in this game will save, and you can't invite other players to the tutorial. Explore, destroy, edit and create to your heart's content! When you are ready to move on and make your first real game, head over to the <a href='/campaigns/new' target='blank'><strong>Create New Game</strong></a> page. If you'd rather join a game on the fly, try <a href='/lfg/search/' target='blank'><strong>looking for a group</strong></a>. <br><br> Happy rolling!","vtt_fg_tour_slide_1_title":"What’s a Foreground Layer?","vtt_fg_tour_slide_1_text":"New for subscribers: Add drama, depth, and detail to your games with a brand new layer.","vtt_fg_tour_slide_2_title":"Interact with Player Tokens!","vtt_fg_tour_slide_2_text":"Drop an art object like a roof or treetop onto the Foreground Layer. When GM or player-controlled tokens intersect with it, the foreground object will automatically <strong>fade</strong>.","vtt_fg_tour_slide_3_title":"Conditional Opacity","vtt_fg_tour_slide_3_text":"Adjust fade opacity in the right-click menu under <strong>Foreground Object</strong>, or turn off Conditional Opacity entirely to obscure tokens. Choose what looks best! ","vtt_fg_tour_slide_4_title":"Tell us what you think!","vtt_fg_tour_slide_4_text":"Read more about the foreground layer <a href='https://help.roll20.net/hc/en-us/articles/30738192036887'>here</a>. ","selected_items_copied":"Items have been copied to clipboar